## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests

**Unit tests** (Vitest — `pnpm --filter @bettracker/core test`):
- `calculations/statistics.test.ts` — All KPI calculations with known inputs/outputs from real CSV data
- `calculations/insights.test.ts` — Insight generator produces correct categories and types
- `calculations/streaks.test.ts` — Streak detection edge cases
- `parsers/betano-parser.test.ts` — Parses both CSV files correctly (includes comma decimals, integer values, typo headers)
- `parsers/parser-factory.test.ts` — Auto-detection selects correct parser
- `validators/*.test.ts` — Zod schema validation (valid + invalid inputs)
- `formatters/*.test.ts` — Currency/date formatting in PT locale

**Integration tests** (Vitest — `pnpm --filter @bettracker/database test`):
- Database queries against test Supabase instance or local Postgres via Docker

**E2E tests** (Playwright — `pnpm --filter web e2e`):
- Auth flow: register → login → redirect to dashboard
- Upload CSV → see KPI values match expected calculations
- Navigate between all pages
- Theme toggle persists across reload
- Export buttons trigger downloads

### Manual Verification

1. **Upload both real CSV files** ([transactions_tomasp2005.csv](file:///c:/Users/tomas/bet-tracker/transactions_tomasp2005.csv) and [transactions_silviatomas.csv](file:///c:/Users/tomas/bet-tracker/transactions_silviatomas.csv)) and verify KPI values match hand calculations
2. **Visual review** of all pages in both dark and light themes at desktop (1920px), tablet (768px), and mobile (375px) widths
3. **Export PDF/PNG/CSV** and confirm output quality + correct data
4. **Auth flow** — test register, login, logout, password reset email

> [!NOTE]
> The test commands above will be finalized during Phase 0 setup when the actual project structure is created. I'll include exact run commands in each phase's implementation.
